# Dave

Hello, I am Dave. I act as a worker, and my job in this session is the
rudimentary method: claims with evidence and credence in the header of every
concept card, the partial logic over them, the cross scores, the north stars,
the typed graph with its schema, the card that describes the graph, the
`methodology/` folder, and the concept card `atom`. My session is
`strange-loops-in-hmd-5e`.

## Report, 02:00

**Goal.** The user asked this session for four things, in this order.

1. A branch `feat/rudimentary` for the rudimentary part of how this will
   work.
2. Front matter on each card that speaks of evidence and probability; claims
   held in the cards and addressable as a list; part of them put into a
   partial logic; a score for every link saying how far its two cards
   disagree, measured in several ways; a dominating cover of abstract
   "north star" concepts; a `methodology/` folder describing the method; one
   document with a D2 diagram of the concepts that tell the story.
3. Each front matter read as an HQL data type that converts to nodes and
   edges, with the type of an edge and its signature checked, and a
   dedicated meta article describing the knowledge graph of the knowledge
   graph, in a strange loop.
4. `atom` as a concept in the logic cluster, not only a term of the
   methodology: an atom may be a long formula in natural language or a
   claim, and it is a mapping from a string to a truth value.

**Done.**

- The branch `feat/rudimentary`, created from `wiki/core-net`.
- Claims on the 51 concept cards that existed then: 356 claims, 243 with an
